        "original_id": "208ecc4f-fec5-5b53-bc16-e4877698650e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sly Stone, Mary Ramsey, Moses Tyson Jr.\n- Bands/Artists: Sly and the Family Stone, Jackson Browne, Goo Goo Dolls, Billy Bragg, Warren Zevon, Alex Chilton, Ani DiFranco\n- Albums/Songs: Playing Favorites, Trouble Me\n- Topics: music careers, collaborations, genre influence\n\nFacts:\n- Sly Stone was born Sylvester Stewart on March 15, 1943, in Denton, Texas.\n- Sly Stone is an American musician, songwriter, and record producer.\n- Sly Stone was the frontman for Sly and the Family Stone.\n- Sly and the Family Stone played a critical role in the development of soul, funk, rock, and psychedelia in the 1960s and 1970s.\n- In 1973, Moses Tyson Jr. started his music career by learning to play guitar by ear so he could be used on a Sly Stone album.\n- Moses Tyson Jr. is Sly Stone's cousin.\n- Mary Ramsey has worked with Jackson Browne, Goo Goo Dolls, Billy Bragg, Warren Zevon, Alex Chilton, and Ani DiFranco.\n- A live version of \"Trouble Me\" with lead vocalist Mary Ramsey was included on the 2016 album \"Playing Favorites\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c966ac21-2418-5451-972b-f57fae1b49d1",
        "text": "Page: Sly Stone. Sentence: Sly Stone (born Sylvester Stewart, March 15, 1943, Denton, Texas) is an American musician, songwriter, and record producer, most famous for his role as frontman for Sly and the Family Stone, a band which played a critical role in the development of soul, funk, rock, and psychedelia in the 1960s and 1970s.\nPage: Mary Ramsey. Sentence: Ramsey has also worked with other well-known artists such as Jackson Browne, Goo Goo Dolls, Billy Bragg, Warren Zevon, Alex Chilton and Ani DiFranco.\nPage: Moses Tyson Jr.. Sentence: He started his music career, in 1973, with learning how to play the guitar by ear in order to be utilized on a Sly Stone album, who is his cousin.\nPage: Trouble Me. Sentence: A live version with lead vocalist Mary Ramsey was also included on their 2016 album \"Playing Favorites\".",
